 \"$P$ and $R$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6af0dc85-88c1-524b-b9f7-d0a62171889c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296860} {:answer/id #uuid "73cf0dd4-2c43-5fce-903b-4db8b67004c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296861} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcab437-aa79-50e9-a57b-7bd6552ab021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296862} {:answer/id #uuid "b16473a4-cdc7-555f-b0d3-dd1bbb8cbc76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296863} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cd0ae9-a896-58e8-8996-703d15aa4c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9cd0ae9-a896-58e8-8996-703d15aa4c24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296864} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d67fb0-1068-58e4-995c-398e06c1d2d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "687f3b06-c801-5d45-8768-11690d2bd814" :question/math-academy-id "q-174415" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:2\\times 28=56$\n\n- $Q:0.2\\in Z$\n\n- $R:\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}$" :question/worked-solution "A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options:\n\n- $P$ is a statement. This statement is *true* because $2$ times  $28$ equals $56.$\n\n- $Q$ is a statement. This statement is *false* because $0.2$ is not an integer.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a statement because it is neither true nor false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4eda1965-d655-5550-9bb5-13e7a9c1b406" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Statements Expressed Using Symbols"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef6a885a-b27b-58d7-89b1-695f41214d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296867} {:answer/id #uuid "1f4940ad-6d83-5dc2-9c26-9d2eaa97bd60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296868} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7e382c-e7f7-5f05-8909-2dc99bfae776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296869} {:answer/id #uuid "31ee4920-6e8b-5bc9-9692-b6d36ee328b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296870} {:answer/id #uuid "f54d22c9-d48d-51ac-8e1b-dc09062b79ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54d22c9-d48d-51ac-8e1b-dc09062b79ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296871} :answer-field/id #uuid "319a39bc-5ad3-5a3d-b72f-4fd65a005561" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28999f73-4e7c-54fe-a133-a9cd91a53853" :question/math-academy-id "q-174416" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical statements?\n\n- $P:{1,2}\\cup {2,3}={1,2,3}$\n\n- $Q:\\frac{1}