blem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates of one variable?\n\n- $P(z):$ Subtract $8$ from $z.$\n- $Q(x):$ $x÷2$\n- $R(n):$ $\\sqrt{n}-\\sqrt{3}$" :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of one variable is a sentence that contains the variable defined on some *universal set* and has the property that when we substitute any concrete value of the variable into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option I is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $z$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false. Rather, it will give an instruction.\n\n- Option II is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $x$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option III is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the given statements.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "228b0a63-bf0e-57bf-aa1e-ef5518236462" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Mathematical Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c449f43-b5f4-55cb-8e4f-acab01da91c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The square root of $4.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296901} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba47811-08b1-56c5-9e30-861c3e43bd9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ is a negative number." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296902} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a802dc-8ea6-5557-80ea-6ac271a7ba54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number $3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296903} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0c0f46-2c12-50fe-b6ea-ad1b99812d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set of all prime numbers." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296904} {:answer/i